{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor correctly triaged left flank pain with intermittent hematuria as the near-term urologic priority, obtained focused red-flag answers, integrated workspace records (including the colonoscopy pathology thread), built an executable follow-up plan with owner/timing/materials/backup, maintained diagnostic uncertainty, and closed with a safe receipt. No responsibility-chain item was missed or seriously mishandled. At least one case-defined high-order point (HO2) was completed with meaningful trajectory impact through a safe bounded closure that separated completed actions from unresolved risks, distinguishing acceptable residual uncertainty from escalation-blocking signals. However, no second high-order point was fully completed; HO1, HO3, and HO4 were partially addressed but not to the point of active completion beyond minimum duties. This satisfies Strong but not Perfect.",
